  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Development Through Traditional Weaving, Natural Dyes, and Expansion of Community Tourism</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AAA will continue to revive the local Andean weaving tradition and will undertake a program of community tourism, thereby benefiting 350 female and male Quechua and Aymara weavers from 19 communities in the department of Cochabamba. AAA will also improve and expand community tourism services it provides in Tapacari and Arque, diversify textile production, and strengthen marketing strategies.</narrative>
  </description>
